Z||000000||William Federle||01-23-2000||07:57 AM||||This question is mainly directed at BATBOY but anyone who has a V8 Fiero might have an answer. Batboy, or anyone, what sort of MPG's do you get on your 2M8? I just saw a question on the other list where some guy had just bought a v8 Fiero and wanted to know so he could plan his trip home. I'm planning to get a v8 some day and I'd like to know too. I guess you have a small block chevy, right?<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 01-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||01-23-2000||09:31 AM||||Yes, my Batmobile has a Chevy 350. I've only measure the gas mileage once. I posted the results here on the Forum at the time. I must have the CRS disease (Can't Remember Schitt). I think it was about 18 mpg. I do remember that out of about 200 miles or so, about 1/2 of that was easy highway miles at 60 mph and the other 1/2 was city driving, showing off, and screwing around. My current engine is pretty much stock, so a modified engine will suck more gas. It's hard to keep your foot out of it when you have all that beautiful noise coming from behind you.||||reg||1
