Z||000013||pherder||01-24-2000||10:52 PM||||I will try to make a long story short ...<P>My first 88 Coupe had a very weak L4.  Didn't matter to me, I was going to make it into a convertible and show it.  Started to strip it down to nothing and found that it had a front clip put on it.  Done well but not show quality.  Picked up an 88 Formula from a salvage yard that had a locked up engine.  Body looked to be in good shape.  Started to tear it apart.  Frame was rusted so bad that the only thing holding the seats in the car was the carpet!!!  Gave away the L4 out of the Coupe and the V6 out of the Formula (yes, gave them away!!!)  Got my 3rd 88 Fiero (my current Project Coupe) with a really bad rod knock.  Engine life measured in seconds!  Took this engine/trans out and put them in the first 88 Coupe that I sold (for $1!!) to George Ryan (Quad 4 Fiero racer).  Gave away bunch of parts and pieces before my move to Kansas and, of course, now need some of the stuff I gave away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>My 88 GT arrived today (George Ryan did a trip and ended up @ my place with the 88 GT) and I will be putting in a 3.1 in it.  I may have extra parts but I may just buy another Fiero to put them in! ;^) (DON'T tell the wife I wrote that!!!)<P>So the bottom line is, I don't have a Fiero's L4 but I do have three V6s for one car ... (2 2.8 and one 3.1 which will use parts from one of the 2.8s).<P>BTW, if you read the thread about Lustine Online parts, I have 8 extra sunroof gaskets and 8 extra right side dew wipes that I will sell ... see the Mart area for info.<P>Paul||||reg||1
